{"content":[{"c":["PISGAH, M",{"c":["ount"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"}],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Mountain located at the northeast end of the Dead Sea near the ancient city of Jericho. Balak took Balaam to the top of Pisgah (",{"href":"?bref=Num.23.14","r":"Num.23.14","rawR":"Num.23.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.23.14","value":"Num.23.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 23:14"},"), and Moses was told to go to its summit to view the Promised Land (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.27","r":"Deut.3.27","rawR":"Deut.3.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.27","value":"Deut.3.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:27"},"). Later, Moses returned to the top of Pisgah to die (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.34.1","r":"Deut.34.1","rawR":"Deut.34.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.34.1","value":"Deut.34.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"34:1"},"). Pisgah’s slopes border the Dead Sea, or Sea of the Arabah (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.17","r":"Deut.3.17","rawR":"Deut.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.17","value":"Deut.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.49","r":"Deut.4.49","rawR":"Deut.4.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.49","value":"Deut.4.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:49"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.3","r":"Josh.12.3","rawR":"Josh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.3","value":"Josh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 12:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.20","r":"Josh.13.20","rawR":"Josh.13.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.20","value":"Josh.13.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:20"},"). The ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," sometimes refers to these slopes as “Ashdoth-pisgah.” Many scholars identify Mt Pisgah with modern Ras es-Siyaghah, just north of Mt Nebo."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=NeboMount_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"NeboMount_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"NeboMount_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Nebo, Mount"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"PisgahMount","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 23:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.23.14","rawQueryValue":"Num.23.14","sourceRefExact":"Num.23.14"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.27","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.27","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.27"},{"anchorText":"34:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.34.1","rawQueryValue":"Deut.34.1","sourceRefExact":"Deut.34.1"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.17","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.17","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.17"},{"anchorText":"4:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.49","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.49","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.49"},{"anchorText":"Jos 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.3","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.3","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.3"},{"anchorText":"13:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.20","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.20","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b8103cdd9265bf6ded01e2dc5cbf5d08f61d043a74c4f068def00bcd5a693781","sourceItemName":"PisgahMount","sourceItemOrder":201,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PisgahMount","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Pisgah, Mount","title":"Pisgah, Mount","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}